adr: 0226
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: constexpr_strings
why: The other direction. §6.8.3.5 pads the shorter value with spaces, which is what makes `'' = ' '` true and `'' < ' '` false. Comparing only the characters that are there makes the shorter value a prefix and therefore *less*, so `'' < ' '` becomes true and `'ab' = 'ab '` false -- and the folder then disagrees with the runtime, which pads. Only a case that compares strings of unequal length can tell, and every equal-length comparison stays green.
--- old
  if ln > rn then n := ln else n := rn;
--- new
  if ln < rn then n := ln else n := rn;
